   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s011-u002",
    "kind": "chant",
    "speakerLabel": "முரசறைவோன்",
    "text": "War! Terrible war! A war that will decide our country's honour—its future! Warriors, make ready! One from every household, set forth! We shall break the bones of the worthless—we shall raise the flag of victory. Come! Come! To war!... War! War! War! Dum, dum, dum!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-011.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-011.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s011-d001",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 23,
       "printed_page": 22
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful",
     "notes": [
      "Classified as chant/proclamation while preserving the immutable labelled source-record link and drum-beat ending."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s011-u003",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வசந்தன்",
    "text": "War! War! Mightiest of warriors! March to war! There are two kinds of war. In one war, cattle graze—that is a hay-war! Another war is merely an akka-war! The war I speak of is the fight in which skulls are smashed! Tiger-eyed warriors! Lions! Leopards! Sheep! Roar and charge! Hmm, set out. Why are you standing there? Cut! Strike down! Kill... rip out their guts......",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-011.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-011.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s011-d002",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 23,
       "printed_page": 22
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful",
     "notes": [
      "Vasanthan's intentionally absurd war-wordplay and descending animal catalogue are preserved rather than regularized."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
